# A loop that spans THREE zones, steered by `warp` (computed goto across zones).
#
# There is no loop syntax. Control just bounces between zones: the grid zone
# decides, each pass, whether to jump back to the printing zone or fall off the
# end and halt. The shared stack carries the counter across every hop.
#
#   zone 0  push the initial counter (runs once)
#   zone 1  print the counter, keeping it on the stack
#   zone 2  a grid: counter -= 1; if it's still > 0, `warp` back to zone 1,
#           otherwise warp to zone 3 -- which doesn't exist, so the program halts
#
# The grid line, left to right:
#   1-      counter - 1
#   :0`     dup, push 0, greater-than  ->  (counter > 0) as 1/0
#   2*3\-   turn that into a warp target: 1 if true (zone 1), 3 if false (halt)
#   &       warp to that target
#   @       stop the grid, handing control back to the driver
{stack 3}
{stack dup .}
{grid
1-:0`2*3\-&@
}
